{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2156-01-08 03:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I know you’re feeling groggy, but I need to go over what happened. Your husband told us you had severe stomach pain after eating toast this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2156-01-08 03:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes… it was sharp, right here." 
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2156-01-08 03:17:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Points to epigastrium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2156-01-08 03:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you felt nauseous too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2156-01-08 03:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. I couldn’t keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2156-01-08 03:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your lipase was 96 when you arrived, which is only slightly high. But your husband said another hospital reported it at 713 earlier today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2156-01-08 03:23:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. That’s why I came here. I was supposed to have an ERCP this week anyway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2156-01-08 03:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Right. Given your history of pancreatitis and sphincter of Oddi dysfunction, we’re watching closely. For now, we’ll keep you NPO—nothing by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2156-01-08 03:26:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Will I get IV fluids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2156-01-08 03:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve already started IV fluids. We’ll also manage your pain carefully."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2156-01-08 03:28:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ve been through this before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2156-01-08 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from last night are stable. White count is normal, liver enzymes are fine. No signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2156-01-08 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about the ERCP? Is it still scheduled?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2156-01-08 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re planning it for tomorrow. We want to make sure you’re stable first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2156-01-08 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this before. It helps when they dilate the duct."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2156-01-08 08:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s why we’re proceeding. We’ll monitor your pain and keep you comfortable until then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2156-01-08 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. How’s the pain now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2156-01-08 14:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there, but better with the meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2156-01-08 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep adjusting as needed. Also, your stool test came back negative for C. diff, so no infection there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2156-01-08 14:34:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had diarrhea the last few days. Is that related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2156-01-08 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. It could be from prior antibiotics or your GI motility issues. We’ll watch it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2156-01-09 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re moving forward with your ERCP today. It’s scheduled for noon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2156-01-09 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Will I be asleep?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2156-01-09 09:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll be under sedation. The goal is to dilate the biliary duct again, since that’s helped before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2156-01-09 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And they’ll check for stones?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2156-01-09 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. The images will show if there are any blockages. But your prior MRCPs were clear, so we don’t expect stones."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2156-01-09 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back. The ERCP went well. They used a balloon to dilate the biliary sphincter—6mm. No stones or blockages found."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2156-01-09 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it was just the dilation?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2156-01-09 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. But that’s what you’ve responded to in the past. The bile flow looks excellent now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2156-01-09 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I already feel a little better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2156-01-09 13:37:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’ll keep you NPO for a few more hours, then start clear liquids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2156-01-09 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2156-01-09 18:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Less pain. Can I try water?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2156-01-09 18:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re starting you on clear liquids. Sip slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2156-01-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news. Your labs this morning are improving. Hemoglobin stable, kidney function normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2156-01-10 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I eat real food today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2156-01-10 08:03:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll try a soft diet—like toast or oatmeal. Start small."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2156-01-10 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had toast last time and got sick… but maybe it’s different now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2156-01-10 08:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "This time your duct is open. That’s the key difference. We’ll monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2156-01-10 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve tolerated the soft diet well. We’ll advance to a regular diet tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2156-01-10 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2156-01-10 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know this is stressful. Your mental health team also reviewed your meds—everything stays the same."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2156-01-10 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. The prazosin helps with nightmares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2156-01-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. Ate breakfast without issues, pain is minimal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2156-01-11 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. I think the procedure helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2156-01-11 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We agree. We’re planning discharge tomorrow morning if all stays on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2156-01-11 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2156-01-11 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take ciprofloxacin for five days—twice a day. It’s precautionary after the ERCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2156-01-11 09:08:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m allergic to some antibiotics. Is cipro safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2156-01-11 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Sulfa and Zofran are your allergies, not cipro. You’re cleared for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2156-01-11 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final labs look great. Hemoglobin stable, electrolytes normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2156-01-11 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my headache from yesterday?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2156-01-11 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely from dehydration or pain meds. It’s gone now, so we don’t think it’s serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2156-01-11 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I get them sometimes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. We’ll update your discharge papers now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. What should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Fever, severe pain, vomiting, or jaundice—those need a call or ER visit. Otherwise, follow up with your GI doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And keep taking ranitidine for reflux?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, same as before. All your meds stay the same except adding cipro for a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure my husband knows."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you printed instructions too. You’re doing well—this episode resolved faster than last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad I came here. I knew I needed the dilation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your instincts were right. We’ll keep coordinating with your GI team for long-term care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you for listening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:18:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2156-01-12 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re all set to go home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2156-01-08 03:15:00",
    "admission_end": "2156-01-12 16:09:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of recurrent abdominal pain and suspected sphincter of Oddi dysfunction presented with acute epigastric pain and nausea after eating, following a reported lipase elevation to 713 at an outside hospital. Upon arrival, her lipase was 96, within her baseline range. She was managed with NPO status, IV fluids, and pain control. An ERCP with biliary sphincteroplasty was performed, showing no stones or blockages but successful dilation of the biliary duct, leading to symptom improvement. She advanced to a regular diet, remained stable, and was discharged home on a short course of ciprofloxacin with instructions to continue her prior medications. Her abdominal pain, nausea, diarrhea, headache, and psychiatric conditions were monitored throughout the stay, with no complications.",
    "problems": [
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Diarrhea",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Headache",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Posttraumatic stress disorder",
      "Problems with hearing",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Nausea alone"
    ]
  }
}
